<title>UK: UK's 3i H1 net asset value rises to 454p/shr.</title>
<headline>UK's 3i H1 net asset value rises to 454p/shr.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.5		    vs 3.1</p>
<p> Pretax revenue profit  62.9		   vs 54.3</p>
<p> Net asset value(pence) 454.0		  vs 426.0</p>
<p> Revenue surplus	  49.8		   vs 42.2</p>
<p> Earnings/share (pence) 8.5		   vs 7.2</p>
<p> Amount invested	  327.3		 vs 324.5</p>
<p> Total return	     188.4		 vs 277.3</p>
<p> Pay date		   January 31, 1997</p>
<p> Div  registration date December 17</p>
<p> Ex-div date		December 9</p>
<p>NOTE - UK investment capital group 3i Group Plc said business confidence had risen in the UK throughout 1996 and it was &quot;continuing to see a good flow of investment opportunities&quot;. It said there was potential for higher levels of investment in continental Europe, where conditions have been less favourable. This would be brought about by economic recovery and &quot;the further development of the private equity markets&quot;.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
